+## Change log — 0.9.8_Hardened_3
+
+**0.9.8_Hardened_3 closes ODR-019.** Option 1 is adopted as diagnostic/tooling
+hardening only. Declaration proximity applies only within the same source
+file; for equal spelling distance, same-file candidates rank before cross-file
+candidates; cross-file ties use canonical qualified-name ordering. No
+project-wide file/module proximity model is introduced. Candidate discovery
+semantics are unchanged, no source program changes validity, and no runtime,
+ABI, ownership, lifetime, overload, import, or type-system semantics change.
+
+| # | Change | Class | Where |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| H3.1 | `[DIA-12]` defines one N1 ranking algorithm: spelling distance, locality class on distance ties, unchanged same-file proximity, canonical qualified identity for cross-file ties, and top-N selection after complete ordering. | DIAGNOSTIC / TOOLING HARDENING | XX.6.2, N1 ranking algorithm |
+| H3.2 | Cross-file identity is independent of unrelated offsets, import/alias positions, filesystem/source discovery, hash iteration, import order, operating-system directory order, and build/cache order; visible suggestion spelling remains unchanged. | DETERMINISTIC DIAGNOSTIC ORDERING | XX.6.2, N1 ranking algorithm |
+| H3.3 | Unit, conformance, and UI regression coverage verifies suggestion order, aliases/imports, inherited fields, prelude candidates, top-three truncation, and repeated runs under reversed file/import discovery order. | IMPLEMENTATION / CONFORMANCE EVIDENCE | `compiler/ember_typeck/src/name_suggestions.rs`, `compiler/ember_driver/tests/ui.rs`, `tests/conformance/DIA-12/` |
+
+**This change log is exhaustive for the 0.9.8_Hardened_3 delta.** The H1
+source-language revision remains the complete 0.9.8 language delta; H2 and H3
+are tooling/diagnostic hardenings.
